# Managed by Ansible (Sovereign fail2ban role).
#
# OpenSSH >= 10.1 penalises misbehaving sources (PerSourcePenalties) and then
# only logs "drop connection ... penalty: ..." for further attempts, which the
# stock filter ignores. Count those drops as failures too, so fail2ban still
# bans sources that sshd throttles. %(known/failregex)s keeps the stock rules.
[Definition]
failregex = %(known/failregex)s
            ^drop connection #\d+ from \[<HOST>\]:\d+ on \S+ penalty: .+$
